        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "06b8d2b0-2fe8-5b1d-8dd5-0704d5e555f5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Heinrich Zimmer, Max Müller, Paul Tillich\n- Roles: German scholar, philologist, Orientalist, philosopher, Indologist\n- Concepts: Indian Philology, Indology, transtheism, theism, atheism, religious philosophy\n\nFacts:\n- Friedrich Max Müller was born on 6 December 1823 and died on 28 October 1900.\n- Max Müller was a German-born philologist and Orientalist who lived and studied in Britain for most of his life.\n- Max Müller wrote both scholarly and popular works on Indology.\n- Heinrich Zimmer was considered the most important German scholar in Indian Philology after Max Müller.\n- Transtheism is a term coined by either Paul Tillich or Heinrich Zimmer.\n- Transtheism refers to a system of thought or religious philosophy that is neither theistic nor atheistic, but beyond both.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
